<h3 id=3D"complexity-analysis">Complexity Analysis</h3>
<p><strong>Time complexity:</strong> The time complexity of <code>build_bin=
ary_tree</code> is <span class=3D"katex"><span class=3D"katex-mathml"><math=
 xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><m=
o stretchy=3D"false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=3D"false">)</mo></mrow><a=
nnotation encoding=3D"application/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics></mat=
h></span><span class=3D"katex-html" aria-hidden=3D"true"><span class=3D"bas=
e"><span class=3D"strut" style=3D"height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></=
span><span class=3D"mord mathnormal" style=3D"margin-right: 0.02778em;">O</=
span><span class=3D"mopen">(</span><span class=3D"mord mathnormal">n</span>=
<span class=3D"mclose">)</span></span></span></span>, as it makes one call =
to the <code>build_subtree</code> function, which recursively traverses eac=
h element in the <code>preorder</code> and <code>inorder</code> arrays once=
, resulting in an <span class=3D"katex"><span class=3D"katex-mathml"><math =
xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo=
 stretchy=3D"false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=3D"false">)</mo></mrow><an=
notation encoding=3D"application/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics></math=
></span><span class=3D"katex-html" aria-hidden=3D"true"><span class=3D"base=
"><span class=3D"strut" style=3D"height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></s=
pan><span class=3D"mord mathnormal" style=3D"margin-right: 0.02778em;">O</s=
pan><span class=3D"mopen">(</span><span class=3D"mord mathnormal">n</span><=
span class=3D"mclose">)</span></span></span></span> runtime.</p>
<p><strong>Space complexity:</strong> The space complexity is <span class=
=3D"katex"><span class=3D"katex-mathml"><math xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/19=
98/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy=3D"false">(</mo><mi=
>n</mi><mo stretchy=3D"false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=3D"applicat=
ion/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=3D"katex-=
html" aria-hidden=3D"true"><span class=3D"base"><span class=3D"strut" style=
=3D"height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class=3D"mord mathn=
ormal" style=3D"margin-right: 0.02778em;">O</span><span class=3D"mopen">(</=
span><span class=3D"mord mathnormal">n</span><span class=3D"mclose">)</span=
></span></span></span> due to the space taken up by the recursive call stac=
k, which can grow as large as the height of the binary tree. The largest po=
ssible height of a binary tree is <span class=3D"katex"><span class=3D"kate=
x-mathml"><math xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mr=
ow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=3D"application/x-tex">n</annotatio=
n></semantics></math></span><span class=3D"katex-html" aria-hidden=3D"true"=
><span class=3D"base"><span class=3D"strut" style=3D"height: 0.4306em;"></s=
pan><span class=3D"mord mathnormal">n</span></span></span></span>. The hash=
 map <code>inorder_indexes_map</code> also takes up <span class=3D"katex"><=
span class=3D"katex-mathml"><math xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/Math=
ML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy=3D"false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo s=
tretchy=3D"false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=3D"application/x-tex">O=
(n)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=3D"katex-html" aria-h=
idden=3D"true"><span class=3D"base"><span class=3D"strut" style=3D"height: =
1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class=3D"mord mathnormal" style=
=3D"margin-right: 0.02778em;">O</span><span class=3D"mopen">(</span><span c=
lass=3D"mord mathnormal">n</span><span class=3D"mclose">)</span></span></sp=
